nking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "Dana's trip is booked. The flight and hotel are on one trip (ID T0003) and both are confirmed.\n\n- **Flight F100** (reservation R0001): SFO to JFK on 2026-11-12, nonstop. At $289, it was the cheapest nonstop option.\n- **Hotel: Harbor Inn, H2** (reservation R0002): check in 2026-11-12 for 2 nights, check out 2026-11-14. Cost is $478 ($239/night).\n- **Total charged to the corporate card:** $767.\n\nThe first booking attempt timed out. Before retrying, I checked Dana's reservations and confirmed nothing had been booked. The retry used the same idempotency key (a reference that stops the system from processing the same booking twice). Dana's reservations now show just these two entries, so there was no double charge.\n\nThe total is under the $1,000 limit that needs manager approval. Even so, the system sent the booking to an approver automatically, and it was approved with the note \"Looks right.\"", "type": "text"}]}]}